From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Euclid Ye <yezhizhenjiakang@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:04:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] backport: deps: Upgrade cookie to 0.18.3 (#50151)

This essentially patches
[RUSTSEC-2026-0594](https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0594.html),
by upgrading cookie to 0.18.3.

We are stuck with 0.16 which is used by webdriver crate still,
but seems we never enable the feature related to the vulnerability
 so it is probably fine.

Testing: test-tidy

Signed-off-by: Euclid Ye <yezhizhenjiakang@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 889914bd6e62c1b17a572dc5e921003276b3e9b5)

----

Fork note: backported onto Servo v0.6.0 for the ohos-v0.6 branch. cargo-deny in test-tidy reports RUSTSEC-2026-0594 (cookie 0.16.2 and 0.18.2) for v0.6.0's lock file; webdriver 0.54.0 holds cookie 0.16 on v0.6.0 too. Cargo.lock conflicted, so it is v0.6.0's with `cargo update -p cookie@0.18.2 --precise 0.18.3`, which changes 20 of upstream's 22 lines: all but upstream's unrelated change to the syn dependency of cssparser-macros.

Validation: On the final stack, at its tip: `./mach test-tidy` (including cargo-deny), `./mach test-scripts`, `./mach clippy --locked -- -- --deny warnings`, the crown build (checked-release, -D warnings, crown built for Rust 1.97.1), `./mach test-unit --profile checked-release` with and without `--doc`, and the OpenHarmony checked-release builds of both flavors with -D warnings, which make signed HAPs, pass; release builds of it with both engines ran the whole WPT suite. cargo-deny passes: the lock file has cookie 0.18.3, and RUSTSEC-2026-0594 stays ignored for webdriver's cookie 0.16, as upstream does.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent cherry-picked upstream commit 889914bd6e6, regenerated its Cargo.lock change with cargo update instead of merging it, and added the fork-style part of this message below the dashed line: fork note, Validation and these trailers)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
